1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,210
I have an idea.

2
00:00:02,250 --> 00:00:04,190
But how do I know

3
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:06,370
what makes it worth watching?

4
00:00:06,990 --> 00:00:08,400
Meet Yuvo.

5
00:00:08,860 --> 00:00:12,910
A creative workspace that turns an idea

6
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:15,160
into a direction you can test.

7
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:18,170
We start with a detective who reads memories

8
00:00:18,170 --> 00:00:20,550
trapped in abandoned buildings.

9
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:23,370
Gemini plans the research.

10
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:26,880
Parallel searches the live web across six angles,

11
00:00:26,990 --> 00:00:28,820
looking for familiar territory

12
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:30,610
and the places nearby stories lose people.

13
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:33,590
This run surfaced fifteen sources.

14
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:37,560
You can open the evidence behind each finding.

15
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:41,500
Gemini connects those signals into a creative opening:

16
00:00:41,910 --> 00:00:45,190
what if the building is an unreliable witness?

17
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:48,910
Each room can remember only its own point of view.

18
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:52,700
Now we have a specific storytelling rule to explore,

19
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:54,840
instead of another vague suggestion.

20
00:00:55,670 --> 00:00:57,930
Next, we attach a real video.

21
00:00:58,330 --> 00:01:02,160
This is stock footage used as an early location test,

22
00:01:02,470 --> 00:01:04,080
not a finished film.

23
00:01:05,260 --> 00:01:07,650
Gemini inspects the frames

24
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:10,970
and returns observations at precise moments.

25
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:13,550
It recognizes the corridor,

26
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:15,670
but points out that the detective

27
00:01:15,670 --> 00:01:18,330
and the conflicting memories are still missing.

28
00:01:18,790 --> 00:01:20,440
Click a timestamp to check the observation yourself.

29
00:01:20,790 --> 00:01:22,640
We attach a second cut.

30
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:25,840
Yuvo sends both videos to Gemini

31
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:28,600
so it can compare what actually changed.

32
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:31,680
The later start changes the framing.

33
00:01:32,260 --> 00:01:34,940
The story still needs a point of view.

34
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:37,360
That is the loop:

35
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:39,900
make a choice, show the cut,

36
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:42,440
and get a concrete next editing move.

37
00:01:42,870 --> 00:01:46,710
Under the hood, Google ADK runs Gemini

38
00:01:46,710 --> 00:01:49,890
three point eight Flash on Vertex AI.

39
00:01:50,190 --> 00:01:52,910
Parallel supplies live research.

40
00:01:53,260 --> 00:01:55,580
The app runs on Google Cloud Run,

41
00:01:55,580 --> 00:01:57,450
with invite-code access

42
00:01:57,450 --> 00:01:59,420
and secrets kept on the server.

43
00:01:59,670 --> 00:02:01,860
The creator keeps the final decision.

44
00:02:02,310 --> 00:02:06,500
Yuvo. Big idea. Better story.

45
00:02:06,856 --> 00:02:09,567
One thoughtful take at a time.
